# Build-context exclusions.
#
# TWO PATTERNS THAT MUST NEVER BE ADDED HERE — both break the build:
#   1. Any blanket markdown pattern (`*.md`, `**/*.md`). backend/pyproject.toml
#      declares `readme = "README.md"`, so hatchling's wheel build inside the
#      second `uv sync` needs backend/README.md present in the context.
#   2. Any lockfile pattern. frontend/package-lock.json feeds `npm ci` and
#      backend/uv.lock feeds `uv sync --frozen`.
# If you are here to "shrink the context further", stop and read the above.

# Secrets — never in an image layer (T-05-01).
#
# `**/` is load-bearing, not belt-and-braces. A root-only `.env*` pattern
# leaves `frontend/.env.local` in the build context, and Next.js reads it at
# BUILD time — baking NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000 into the
# static bundle. The container then serves a frontend that asks the
# *browser's* localhost for its API, which works by accident on a developer's
# machine and fails with ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED anywhere else. Caught by the
# E2E suite; invisible to every curl-based check before it.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# A developer's live database would otherwise be baked into image history
# (T-05-02). The container's DB lives on the mounted volume instead.
db/
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-journal

# Dependency trees and build output — reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/.venv
frontend/out
frontend/.next

# Python/tooling caches.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# VCS, tooling, and planning material — none of it is needed at runtime.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.planning
planning
test
scripts
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
